# Custom Widgets & DRY

Prefer existing widgets/utils over one-off Material rebuilds. If the same UI appears twice, extract to `lib/widgets/<type>/`.

## Required building blocks

| Need | Use | Path |
|------|-----|------|
| Text | `TextWidget` | `widgets/text/text_widget.dart` |
| Rich / legal text | `CustomRichText` | `widgets/text/custom_rich_text.dart` |
| Primary CTA | `CustomButton` | `widgets/button/custom_button.dart` |
| Link / skip | `CustomTextButton` | `widgets/button/text_button.dart` |
| Form field | `CustomTextField` | `widgets/text_field/custom_text_field.dart` |
| Tappable bordered box | `CustomContainer` | `widgets/common/custom_container.dart` |
| Onboarding options | `SelectableContainer` / `WhatLikeContainer` | `widgets/container/` |
| Snackbars | `ShortMessageUtils` | `core/utils/short_message.dart` |
| Spacing | `AppSize.h*` / `w*` / `getHeight` | `core/utils/app_size.dart` |
| Validation | `Validators.*` | `core/utils/validators.dart` |
| Date/time pickers | `CommonUtils.*` | `core/utils/common_utils.dart` |

Also prefer: `InsightContainer`, `RecommendationCard`, `AttentionContainer`, `CustomCheckbox`, `OnboardingHeader`, `DrawerTile`, home headers under `widgets/header/` and `widgets/home/`.

## Examples

```dart
// ❌ BAD
Text('Continue', style: TextStyle(fontSize: 15, fontWeight: FontWeight.w500));
ElevatedButton(onPressed: onTap, child: Text('Continue'));
ScaffoldMessenger.of(context).showSnackBar(...);
Padding(padding: EdgeInsets.all(16), …);

// ✅ GOOD
TextWidget(title: 'Continue');
CustomButton(title: 'Continue', onTap: onTap);
ShortMessageUtils.showSuccess(context, msg);
Padding(padding: EdgeInsets.all(AppSize.getHeight(16)), …);
// or AppSize.h2 / AppSize.w5 where those helpers fit
```

## Anti-patterns

- Raw `Text` / `ElevatedButton` / ad-hoc fields for standard app UI
- Hardcoded colors/paths/spacing when `AppColors` / `AppImages` / `AppSize` exist
- Duplicating selection rows instead of `SelectableContainer` / `WhatLikeContainer`
- New state/routing libs (Riverpod, Bloc, go_router) — stick to GetX + `AppPages`
- Treating stubs as real UI (`QuickStepContainer` is a `Placeholder`)

## When adding a widget

1. Put it under `lib/widgets/<type>/`
2. Name `custom_*.dart` or a clear descriptive name
3. Parameterize colors via `AppColors` / theme; assets via `AppImages`
4. Reuse `TextWidget` / `AppSize` inside the new widget
